---
/** Plain-language affiliate disclosure. Linked from every AffiliateCta and the footer. */
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AffiliateCta from '~/components/domain/AffiliateCta.astro';
import DocShell from '~/components/static/DocShell.astro';
import AsideCard from '~/components/static/AsideCard.astro';
import { CONTACT, LEGAL_ENTITY, SITE_NAME } from '~/config/site';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from '~/components/static/content';

Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=60, s-maxage=600');

const toc = [
  { id: 'money', label: 'How we make money' },
  { id: 'labels', label: 'Which links are affiliate' },
  { id: 'clicks', label: 'How clicks are counted' },
  { id: 'independence', label: 'What partnerships never change' },
  { id: 'non-paying', label: 'Apps that pay us nothing' },
  { id: 'questions', label: 'Questions' },
];
const site = Astro.site ?? Astro.url;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL('/', site).href },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 2,
        name: `Affiliate disclosure · ${SITE_NAME}`,
        item: new URL('/affiliate-disclosure', site).href,
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: `Affiliate disclosure · ${SITE_NAME}`,
    url: new URL('/affiliate-disclosure', site).href,
    description: `How ${SITE_NAME} earns money from affiliate links, how every one is labelled, and why partnerships never change what we detect or rank.`,
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} earns money from affiliate links, how every one is labelled, and why partnerships never change what we detect or rank.`}
  canonical="/affiliate-disclosure"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <DocShell
    title="Affiliate disclosure"
    eyebrow="Trust"
    lede="Some links to apps and themes earn us a commission. Every one is labelled, and none of them changes our data."
    updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
    toc={toc}
    current="/affiliate-disclosure"
  >
    <Fragment slot="summary">
      <ul>
        <li>Affiliate links say “Affiliate link” right under the button.</li>
        <li>
          They pass through <code>/go/…</code>, which counts clicks per day and stores nothing about
          you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Detections, counts, rankings and comparisons are the same whether an app pays us or not.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <h2 id="money">How we make money</h2>
    <p>
      Today, {SITE_NAME} earns money in one way: affiliate commissions. When you follow one of our
      links to an app or a theme and then pay for it, the developer may pay us a share. The price
      you pay is the same. Commissions are paid to {LEGAL_ENTITY}, which runs {SITE_NAME}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Later we will add <a href="/pro">Pro</a>, a paid plan for designers and agencies. We don’t
      sell data, and we don’t sell placements in our lists.
    </p>

    <h2 id="labels">Which links are affiliate</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate links only appear on outbound buttons to an app listing, a theme page or a
      developer’s site. Each one carries the label right under it, and the link is marked{' '}
      <code>rel="sponsored"</code> for search engines. Links without a partnership say so too.
    </p>
    <figure class="label-demo">
      <div class="label-demo__row" inert aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="label-demo__cell">
          <p class="label-demo__kind">Affiliate link</p>
          <AffiliateCta
            href="/affiliate-disclosure"
            label="View on App Store"
            isAffiliate
            size="md"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="label-demo__cell">
          <p class="label-demo__kind">Ordinary link</p>
          <AffiliateCta
            href="/affiliate-disclosure"
            label="View on App Store"
            isAffiliate={false}
            size="md"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Both buttons as they appear on app and theme pages. The line under each one says which kind
        it is.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2 id="clicks">How clicks are counted</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate links point to a short address on our site, <code>/go/</code> followed by a number.
      When you click one, we add one to that link’s total for the day and send you straight on to
      the partner. We store the link, the date and the count, and nothing that identifies you: no IP
      address, no cookie, no account.
    </p>
    <p>
      The partner’s site may set its own cookie to credit the referral. That happens on their site,
      under their privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="independence">What partnerships never change</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>What we detect on a store, and when.</li>
      <li>How many stores an app or theme is seen on, its share and its rank.</li>
      <li>The order of lists, comparisons and alternatives.</li>
      <li>App Store ratings, reviews and prices, which we copy as published.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Partners can’t pay to be listed, ranked higher or described differently, and they don’t see
      our editorial copy before it’s published.
    </p>

    <h2 id="non-paying">Apps that pay us nothing</h2>
    <p>
      Many of the most-used apps, such as Klaviyo and Judge.me, have no affiliate program with us.
      They appear exactly as they would if they did: same counts, same rank, same screenshots, with
      an ordinary link to their listing. If an app is on a store, we show it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Partnerships change over time. The label next to each link is always the current truth for
      that link.
    </p>

    <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
    <p>
      If something looks like it was influenced by a partnership, tell us at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.hello}`}>{CONTACT.hello}</a>. The{' '}
      <a href="/methodology">methodology</a> explains how every number is made.
    </p>

    <Fragment slot="aside">
      <AsideCard title="How numbers are made">
        <p>
          Detection, shares and dates, in plain words. <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a>
        </p>
      </AsideCard>
    </Fragment>
  </DocShell>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .label-demo {
    margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-2);
  }
  .label-demo__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--line);
  }
  .label-demo__cell {
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .label-demo__kind {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }
  .label-demo :global(.btn) {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .label-demo figcaption {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .label-demo__row {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
